notes="Sheet headed EZ 3, numbered361. It records associativity of shuffle and A-W, shuffle anticommutativity and A-W commutativity up to homotopy, followed by a trisimplicial diagram. The left parenthesis groups two lines; the right integral connector lacks a head. A badly cancelled tensor trial may have three factors, so its count remains uncertain, while its arrow is readable. The middle comparison has a wave over a crossed right arrow, not a clean isomorphism. The normalization tildes sit on Z. Three Hom exponents are single prime-like strokes. The quoted German title is Ueber Steenrodsche operationen, left unfinished; the reference is transcribed, not researched. The two final Hom expressions have unfinished outer parentheses and a separate right brace. The qualification pour X variable is inserted beneath the claim of a free resolution, and the final verb is tronque. The qualification is mathematically essential: for fixed X=point, the usual normalized chain complex is Z in degree0, so the corresponding fixed-X Hom complex is Z in degree0 with trivial symmetric-group action. For n at least2 it cannot be a free Z[Sigma_n] module, whose underlying rank is a multiple of n!. This checks why the text cannot safely be read as an unqualified fixed-X assertion; it does not refute or prove the intended natural-operation theorem. No proof of the asserted shuffle/A-W properties or the Dold theorem is supplied here. No date."
